":"If Portola Valley were to lose our Town status, we would lose local control over important decisions that affect I t","x":172,"y":701,"w":2113,"h":44},{"text":"our community, including zoning and land use. Instead of decisions being made in our Town these decisions 17","x":171,"y":750,"w":2101,"h":45},{"text":"could be made by County.","x":170,"y":801,"w":488,"h":42},{"text":"5","x":2225,"y":806,"w":27,"h":31},{"text":"YES on \"","x":169,"y":901,"w":182,"h":33},{"text":"prevents a County takeover of our local zoning and planning services.","x":474,"y":898,"w":1303,"h":43},{"text":"EMERGENCY RESPONSE & PREPAREDNESS","x":171,"y":997,"w":924,"h":36},{"text":"\" ensures Portola Valley is prepared for natural disasters such as wildfires, earthquakes, flooding 15","x":425,"y":1094,"w":1887,"h":43},{"text":"YES on \"","x":168,"y":1097,"w":182,"h":33},{"text":"or landslides with prevention measures, evacuation planning and emergency response communication","x":169,"y":1144,"w":1922,"h":43},{"text":"systems.","x":170,"y":1197,"w":164,"h":41},{"text":"Maintains wildfire prevention services including vegetation and brush management and","x":473,"y":1291,"w":1626,"h":42},{"text":"YES on \"","x":168,"y":1294,"w":182,"h":33},{"text":"clearance programs reducinq the chance of wildfires.","x":169,"y":1340,"w":1045,"h":43},{"text":"YES on \"","x":167,"y":1441,"w":182,"h":33},{"text":"• Maintains 911 emergency response times and police patrols","x":239,"y":1492,"w":1194,"h":42},{"text":"• Repairs deteriorating storm drains preventing flooding and water pollution q","x":239,"y":1543,"w":1499,"h":43},{"text":"Provide community resilence 3","x":310,"y":1596,"w":601,"h":42},{"text":"LOCAL CONTROL OVER PORTOLA VALLEY'S FUNDING","x":169,"y":1694,"w":1140,"h":34},{"text":"5","x":1339,"y":1694,"w":27,"h":30},{"text":"13","x":2243,"y":1296,"w":38,"h":32},{"text":"\" requires every dime be used for Town services—none can be taken by the County, 2-0","x":583,"y":1742,"w":1668,"h":43},{"text":"By law, YES on \"","x":182,"y":1744,"w":328,"h":42},{"text":"gives you—the Portola Valley taxpayer LOCAL CONTROL.","x":992,"y":1791,"w":1142,"h":43},{"text":"State or Federal Government. Yes on \"","x":168,"y":1792,"w":725,"h":35},{"text":"\" ACCOUNTABILITY 3","x":487,"y":1890,"w":477,"h":35},{"text":"MEASURE \"","x":169,"y":1892,"w":244,"h":33},{"text":"includes strict accountability provisions, including public spending reports, community oversight 13","x":425,"y":1939,"w":1850,"h":42},{"text":"Yes on \"","x":167,"y":1941,"w":158,"h":33},{"text":"and annual independent financial audits. Additionally, all funds go ONLY to Portola Valley, and none can be 16","x":168,"y":1988,"w":2103,"h":43},{"text":"taken by the state.","x":167,"y":2040,"w":345,"h":42},{"text":"4","x":2223,"y":2050,"w":25,"h":28},{"text":"We must take action now if we want to save our Town. Join Portola Valley firefighters, local business owners, 18","x":167,"y":2136,"w":2118,"h":43},{"text":"a unanimous City Council and your neighbors and vote YES on \"","x":167,"y":2186,"w":1221,"h":43},{"text":"Signers:","x":168,"y":2286,"w":152,"h":42},{"text":"Brenda Lane Munks 3","x":168,"y":2335,"w":431,"h":37},{"text":"Nancy Lund","x":169,"y":2385,"w":223,"h":42},{"text":"2","x":566,"y":2390,"w":23,"h":28},{"text":"Former Mayor Gary Nielsen 4","x":169,"y":2433,"w":571,"h":43},{"text":"Town Trails and Paths Committee Member Fred Leach","x":167,"y":2482,"w":1030,"h":35},{"text":"Rita Comes Whitney 3","x":169,"y":2532,"w":469,"h":42},{"text":"Iota( .","x":1775,"y":2627,"w":179,"h":40},{"text":"ZI","x":659,"y":2653,"w":42,"h":33},{"text":"1)","x":2238,"y":2212,"w":21,"h":28},{"text":"104","x":2291,"y":2284,"w":76,"h":34},{"text":"300","x":1985,"y":2626,"w":93,"h":39}]}]}
